WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.310
Let's go next to our caller from the nine
five one area code.

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:09.290
Who's calling today from nine five one and,
uh, where are you calling from?

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:14.690
Hi, my name is Lisa and I'm calling from southern
California.

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:17.510
All right, Lisa, what's on your mind today?

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:18.510
Okay.

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:24.160
I wanted to address the issue of the Census
and the new question about citizenship.

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:25.160
Yes.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:32.349
Um, this was a topic that interested me very
much during our last, then since in 2010 and

00:00:32.349 --> 00:00:33.840
I did a lot of research on it.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:42.370
And the fact is that the US Census Bureau
is authorized to do a head count and that's

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:43.370
it.

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:46.210
All those questions are voluntary.

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:48.460
You don't have to answer any of them.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:50.460
That's right.

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:51.469
Yeah.

00:00:51.469 --> 00:00:55.579
And so, you know, if somebody doesn't want
to answer their citizenship questions, they

00:00:55.579 --> 00:00:56.579
don't have to.

00:00:56.579 --> 00:01:00.020
When I filled out my census forms, I didn't
even give our names.

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:02.739
I just gave them how many people were in my
house.

00:01:02.739 --> 00:01:07.049
I told them our ages cause I believe that's
important for the congress people to know

00:01:07.049 --> 00:01:13.170
there, you know, the, the, their constituency,
the, you know, and I'm also, I gave her income

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:17.720
level because you know, they should know what
services they need to provide as far as kids'

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:21.990
education and senior services and that.

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:25.920
But all those other questions, I left blank

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:31.700
that you know, that, but I'm sure, I'm guessing
that you, so this is an argument for the citizenship

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:35.909
questions shouldn't be on there or is this
an argument for who cares if it's on there?

00:01:35.909 --> 00:01:37.170
People don't have to answer it,

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:38.170
right?

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:39.170
Yeah,

00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:40.170
no.

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:41.170
Which of which are the two?

00:01:41.170 --> 00:01:42.479
Which of the two are you arguing?

00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:46.990
Um, the one that, that, um, people don't have
to answer it.

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:47.990
Yes.

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:48.990
No, I know people.

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:49.990
Right.

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:53.009
But the problem is Lisa Jay, not everybody
is going to hear this phone call.

00:01:53.009 --> 00:01:56.049
Not Everybody is going to get the message
about voluntary questions.

00:01:56.049 --> 00:02:00.530
So the problem is that when you put that question
on there, the whole point of it is that it's

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:05.110
going to dissuade certain people from filling
out the census at all, which will mean those

00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:06.930
populations are under counted.

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:08.340
So I completely agree with you.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:12.610
You don't have to answer it, but it's still
extremely problematic to include the question

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:16.360
and hopefully the, the legal action to try
to stop it will succeed.

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:20.910
Well, I think we need to get the word out
that people don't need to.

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:25.870
I mean, the Census Bureau has no legal authority
to compel anyone.

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:27.099
Yes, I agree.

00:02:27.099 --> 00:02:30.620
We've got to get the word out, but you know,
there's 340 million people in this country

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:34.090
and most of them are not going to get that
word and it's certainly not going to come,

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:39.959
uh, a front and center, uh, from the current,
uh, um, administration, that's for sure.

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:45.590
But you're absolutely right, Lisa, and I appreciate
you calling in and, uh, making that call.

00:02:45.590 --> 00:02:46.590
On that note.

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:47.590
Yeah,

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:48.590
let me go to a break.

00:02:48.590 --> 00:02:49.590
Sorry.

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:50.590
Yet to everybody I didn't get to.

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:51.590
We will take live calls again.

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:51.870
Appreciate you calling it

